# S15c: the game's very first view, in the Classic preset as it ships. The start map, the
# player at its spawn (544,288,32, yaw 90), its own eye, not moving, QUAKE carved over the
# arch. 960x600 in the 4:3 box, id's status bar 1:1, the gun, id's 72 Hz frame gate on a
# 60 Hz screen (`display 4:3 60`; with no screen a 60 fps film would never show one tick
# in six), id's mixer at 11025 Hz, Brightness 0.8. Only the flames, the sky and the lava
# move. 23 s with a second of handle each end. S15c and S15s share one clock: file frame k
# is the same game second in both, so the film cuts from one to the other at the same file
# time.
#
# Under V4-11, "Switch them all off, and you get Classic: id's game.", and V3-12, "How do
# you prove a port is faithful?" (S16).
#
# Assembly (S15, S16): S15 is S15s alone from file second 1.0. S16 takes both files from
# file second 19.0 (the camera never moves, so the later frames show the same view): it
# opens on S15s, black pillars close in to the 4:3 box over 0.4 s (eased), and on the
# closed box the picture is S15c, with the edit's "Classic" label at the box's top left
# and id's menu sound on the switch.

map start

duration 25
fps 60
size 1920x1080

preset classic
display 4:3 60
hud on
gun on
cvar gamma 0.8

camera player

sound on
events on
